      "value": "I have had to remove people in my friend group from my friends list before to be willing to go green/blue, sometimes temporarily, and the fact that this is not public info meant I only had to explain myself to them - people can be nosy. (I have stayed friends with them on Discord, the meaning of \"friend\" there is very different.) Also, without privacy controls, this makes it obvious if someone avoids adding one person in particular, both to that person and to the friend group.\n\nIn general, I think this could be a nice feature, but it could also create pressures to add (and then not remove) people who you don't actually want joining you, which could in turn push people further away from joinable statuses. I think privacy controls are required at a minimum (Discord has none), as well as thought about whether these dynamics can be mitigated. (For example, this would be less of an issue if you could set your status colour per group of friends.)\n\nOne last thing: if this is available on the website, and people start tracking it (as we know people do) and making feeds of who friended or unfriended who, that removes the need for people to even notice changes themselves.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
